ad of a concrete maximum number of consecutive loan renewals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate item eligibility within 2 seconds and issue the loan receipt\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Only specifies the happy path; omits required error handling and user feedback when item eligibility validation fails or a barcode scan is invalid.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-014\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_value_or_unit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the allowed maximum number of active hold requests\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Refers to 'the allowed maximum number of active hold requests' without defining the numeric cap anywhere in the specification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"borrow up to 8 physical items simultaneously\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-009\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-009, which limits an active Member in good standing to at most 5 physical items checked out simultaneously rather than 8.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-016\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"21 calendar days\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-010\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-010, which sets the standard loan duration for circulating print books to 14 calendar days rather than 21 calendar days.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-017\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"self-register online with only an email address and immediately check out physical books without Librarian ID verification\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-001\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-001, which requires a Librarian to verify government-issued photo ID and record full name, email address, and phone number before creating a Member account.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-018\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"remain held indefinitely until the requesting Member explicitly cancels the hold\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-011\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-011, which specifies holding reserved items on the pickup shelf for exactly 72 hours before automatically canceling the hold.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-021\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"coordination\",\n      \"evidence\": \"send an overdue email and/or suspend borrowing privileges and/or apply a penalty flag\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Chained 'and/or' connectives make it ambiguous which exact combination of the three actions must be performed when an item is 7 days overdue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-022\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall be reviewed, approved, and recorded\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without specifying which actor or system role (e.g., Librarian, Administrator) is responsible for reviewing, approving, and recording fine waiver requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-023\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"if appropriate\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The weak phrase 'if appropriate' is subjective and leaves undefined the concrete conditions and lead time for dispatching SMS due-date alerts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-024\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TBD years\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved 'TBD' placeholder instead of a concrete retention period for payment receipts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-025\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"$1.25 USD per overdue day per item with no maximum cap\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-019\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-019, which specifies an overdue fine of $0.50 USD per overdue day per item capped at a maximum of $20.00 USD per item.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-026\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"renew borrowed items online at any time regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-020\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-020, which blocks any Member with an unpaid fine balance exceeding $5.00 USD from borrowing or renewing items.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-027\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Patron's active loan count and enforce the 5-item borrowing limit on the Patron profile screen\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-001\",\n        \"SD-009\",\n        \"SD-015\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Introduces the undefined term 'Patron' instead of the consistent term 'Member' used in earlier requirements (e.g., SD-001, SD-009); its '5-item borrowing limit' also conflicts with the 8-item limit in SD-015.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-028\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"quickly even when many users\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'quickly' and 'many users' are vague, unquantified terms that lack specific response-time thresholds and concurrent user load targets.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-029\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"where possible\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The weak phrase 'where possible' is subjective and non-testable because it does not define the exact conditions under which query-term highlighting is required.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-030\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"sufficient ISBN matching accuracy and acceptable response times\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'sufficient' and 'acceptable' are subjective terms that omit measurable accuracy percentages and maximum response-time bounds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-031\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"efficiently process large batch MARC21 files without noticeable system slowdown\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'efficiently', 'large', and 'noticeable system slowdown' are vague and unmeasurable without specified file sizes, throughput targets, and acceptable latency degradation limits.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-032\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the Catalog Service shall detect the active references\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies only that active loans or holds must be detected upon a deletion attempt, omitting the required resulting action (e.g., blocking deletion and returning an error).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-034\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"at TBD intervals\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved 'TBD' placeholder instead of a concrete schedule interval for full database backups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-035\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"important administrative actions in a timely manner and retain them for an appropriate period\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'important', 'in a timely manner', and 'an appropriate period' are vague terms that fail to define which actions must be audited, maximum logging latency, and exact retention duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-036\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the Failover Manager shall log event FAILOVER-01\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Only specifies logging event FAILOVER-01 when the primary database node is unreachable, omitting the required failover or recovery actions (e.g., promoting a standby node or alerting operators).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-037\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"adequate transport security and clear error messages\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'adequate' and 'clear' are subjective terms that omit concrete transport security standards (e.g., TLS version) and verifiable criteria for authentication error messages.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-038\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"any Member password of at least 8 characters\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-002\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-002, which requires Member passwords of at least 12 characters containing uppercase, lowercase, and numeric characters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-039\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"60 minutes of user inactivity\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-004\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-004, which terminates authenticated web portal sessions after 15 minutes of user inactivity rather than 60 minutes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-040\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"encrypt all Member passwords using reversible AES-256 encryption so Administrators can decrypt\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-003\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-003, which mandates one-way bcrypt hashing (cost factor 12) for all Member and Librarian passwords and forbids storing plaintext passwords.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","duration_seconds":181.332297,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":12898,"output_tokens":24652,"thinking_tokens":21466,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":37550}}}
